// Permit Access if a Grant with role "admin" happened within the
// last hour for any user. The predicate pins `role` to the entity
// literal `Drupe::Grant_Input_role::"admin"` and omits `user`
// (wildcarding it). This exercises:
//   1. Entity-literal constant matching in predicate fields.
//   2. Correct serialization of the entity `Type::"id"` format in
//      the SQL WHERE clause comparison.
//   3. Wildcarding of the omitted `user` field.
//
// The trace has two Grant events: one granting "reader" and one
// granting "admin". Only the admin grant should satisfy the predicate.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Access",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Grant"::request{ input.role: Drupe::Grant_Input_role::"admin" }
};
